# Local only, never committed:
# - .venv: an old venv inside the repo. The shared venv now lives at
#   %USERPROFILE%\venvs\ee475-cnn (TensorFlow's paths are too long in here);
#   each computer builds its own from the requirements.txt files
# - __pycache__ / *.pyc: written by Python automatically
# - data: recorded takes are shared outside git (team decision, 2026-11-18)
# - logs: GUI logs; attach a specific log as test evidence when one is asked for
# - training/runs: train.py and windows.py run folders (owner, 2026-11-22),
#   including train.py --synthetic's made-up clips; keep the ones worth keeping
#   elsewhere. firmware-bench/model_data.h, which train.py also writes, IS
#   committed: the firmware needs it to build
# - training/sample_data: left by the retired request-3 sample set (git tag
#   pre-manual-overhaul), so an old copy is never committed
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/
logs/
training/runs/
training/sample_data/
